I go to the kitchen.
I make two cups of black tea.
The tea is very hot.
I bring the tea into the living room.
Anitha is in the living room.
She sits in a big chair.
I give a cup to her.
I sit on the sofa near her.
My sandals lie under the sofa.
We drink the hot tea.
"This tea is very good," Anitha says.
"Thank you," I say.
We talk.
"This building is very quiet," I say.
"Yes, this is a good building," Anitha says.
The new plant sits near the window.
There is a good breeze in the room.
We put the cups on top of the table.
